        "sign_ahQcpG": {
          "type": "sign",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "You Are Living in the Most Fragile Skeleton in Human History",
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/bone-mass.jpg",
            "image_alt": "",
            "body": "<p>Hunter-gatherers living 7,000 years ago carried roughly 20% more bone mass than modern humans. Their bones were as strong as an orangutan's. Bronze Age women had 5% to 10% more arm-bone strength than modern female athletes.</p><p>Every ancestor scientists have scanned, from early humans to Neanderthals, had denser bone than you. We did not evolve into stronger bodies. We civilized ourselves into weaker ones.</p>",
            "close_text": "Your grandparents felt it at 60. Your parents felt it at 50. Now people negotiate with their knees in their 40s. If the line keeps dropping, what happens to your children?",
            "show_inline_cta": false,
            "inline_cta_text": "",
            "inline_cta_label": "See the one thing built to get in",
