        "sign_K8Ud8t": {
          "type": "sign",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Joint Rot Does Not Damage One Cell and Stop",
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/joint-rot-spread-1x1.gif",
            "image_alt": "",
            "body": "<p>This is the part that should light a fire under you. Oxidation attacks one joint cell, tears it open, and sets off the cell beside it. Then that cell attacks the next. The damage moves through healthy tissue one row at a time, like something with teeth.</p><p>It eats the fluid that cushions the joint. It weakens the tissue that holds everything in line. It turns morning stiffness into the handrail, the brace, the cane, and the list of things you quietly stopped doing.</p>",
            "close_text": "You do not feel a single bite until enough damage has already been done. Every day you wait gives it another row of cells.",
            "show_inline_cta": false,
            "inline_cta_text": "",
            "inline_cta_label": "See the one thing built to get in",
            "testimonial_1_initial": "",
            "testimonial_1_text": "",
