        "sign_Qf7NKL": {
          "type": "sign",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "One Red Molecule Is Shaped to Get Inside the Wall",
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/molecule-transmembrane-1x1.gif",
            "image_alt": "",
            "body": "<p>Its name is astaxanthin. It is the deep red pigment microalgae make when the sun turns brutal and their water begins to disappear. The algae flood their own cells with it so they do not burn up and die.</p><p>Most antioxidants guard one side of the cell membrane. Astaxanthin threads through the entire wall, with one end facing out and one end facing in. Scientists call it a transmembrane antioxidant.</p><p>In antioxidant assays, astaxanthin measures up to <strong>6,000 times stronger than vitamin C.</strong></p>",
            "close_text": "Raw strength is not the most important part. It gets where joint rot lives and breaks the chain before the next cell falls.",
            "show_inline_cta": false,
            "inline_cta_text": "",
            "inline_cta_label": "See the one thing built to get in",
            "testimonial_1_initial": "",
